          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.787,
            0.723,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": "**Sodium and chloride ions, being oppositely charged, attract each other and are held by strong electrostatic forces of attraction to exist as sodium chloride (NaCl). It should be noted that sodium chloride does not exist as molecules but aggregates of oppositely charged ions.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.851,
            0.722,
            0.883
          ],
          "content": "**Let us see the formation of one more ionic compound, magnesium chloride (Fig. 3.6).**"
        },
